    "answer": "Customer 1500 is flagged as a repeat disputer, so you should dispute this claim and not just accept it.\n\nIn the last 90 days (since about 2026-07-26), this customer has six refunded marketplace orders. Each was refunded in full:\n- DoorDash, Oct 13, $33.84\n- DoorDash, Sep 18, $33.21\n- DoorDash, Sep 13, $73.39\n- Uber Eats, Sep 10, $39.17\n- Uber Eats, Aug 30, $31.21\n- DoorDash, Aug 4, $136.67\n\nThe policy flags any customer with three or more refunded marketplace orders in 90 days. For flagged customers, every missing-item claim is disputed whatever the order value, and you, as the owner, are told [marketplace: Repeat disputes]. Consider this notice that the flag applies.\n\nThe dispute has to be filed inside the platform's window, counted from the order date. That is 7 days for DoorDash, 30 for Uber Eats and 14 for Grubhub. A late dispute is rejected automatically [marketplace: Missing or incorrect items]. Check which platform and date the new order is on. Today is Oct 24, so a DoorDash order from Oct 13 is already past its window.\n\nThe platform refunds the customer and charges the cost back to you by default. A packing photo of the item in the bag is the evidence for a dispute. Photos are taken for every marketplace order over $40. The rule for an order over $40 with no photo is to accept the chargeback and log it as a packing miss. The flag rule says to dispute regardless of value, so I can't tell you which of the two wins for a flagged order over $40 with no photo. You'd need to decide that.\n\nI don't know which order the new claim is about, so I can't check its date or amount.",
